---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Reveal from "../components/Reveal.astro";
import "../styles/base.css";
import "../styles/pages/research.css";
---

<Base title={"Research · Y2O"} description={"The public data behind Y2O: grades compressing, skills shifting, youth pathways under pressure. Every number links to its source."} current="/research">
<header class="hero" style="padding-bottom: 90px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="tag rv">Research base</span>
    <h1 class="rv d1">
      The numbers shaping <em>youth, school, and work</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="sub rv d2">
      Y2O is a product, not a study. Every claim on this site links to a
      public source.
    </p>
    <div class="actions rv d3">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="contact.html">Create your account</a
      ><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#sources">See the sources</a>
    </div>
    <div class="src-strip rv d3">
      <a
        href="https://www.weforum.org/publications/the-future-of-jobs-report-2025/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        >World Economic Forum</a
      >
      <a href="https://www.oecd.org/pisa/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >OECD</a
      >
      <a
        href="https://search.open.canada.ca/qpnotes/record/esdc-edsc%2CFCY_JUN2025_005"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        >Government of Canada</a
      >
      <a
        href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/get-your-high-school-volunteer-hours"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        >Ontario Ministry of Education</a
      >
      <a
        href="https://www.fraserinstitute.org/commentary/grade-inflation-gives-students-false-sense-of-their-academic-abilities"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        >Fraser Institute</a
      >
      <a
        href="https://uwaterloo.ca/engineering/future-students"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
        >University of Waterloo</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="sec dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag on-dark">The case</span>
      <h2 class="h2">What the public data shows</h2>
      <p class="lead">Four numbers we keep coming back to.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="four">
      <div class="chg rv">
        <div class="big">914<em>K</em></div>
        <h4>Youth off track</h4>
        <p>Canadians 15 to 29 not in school, work, or training.</p>
        <a
          href="https://search.open.canada.ca/qpnotes/record/esdc-edsc%2CFCY_JUN2025_005"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >Government of Canada / ESDC, 2025</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="chg rv d1">
        <div class="big">39<em>%</em></div>
        <h4>Skills are changing</h4>
        <p>Of workers' core skills, by 2030.</p>
        <a
          href="https://www.weforum.org/publications/the-future-of-jobs-report-2025/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >World Economic Forum, 2025</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="chg rv d2">
        <div class="big">87<em>%</em></div>
        <h4>Grades compressed</h4>
        <p>UBC average entrance grade, up from 70%.</p>
        <a
          href="https://www.fraserinstitute.org/commentary/grade-inflation-gives-students-false-sense-of-their-academic-abilities"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >Fraser Institute, 2024</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="chg rv d3">
        <div class="big">40<em>h</em></div>
        <h4>The legal floor</h4>
        <p>Community involvement needed to graduate in Ontario.</p>
        <a
          href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/get-your-high-school-volunteer-hours"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >Ontario Ministry of Education</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag">The shift</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Grades compress, so the record has to do more</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        When top grades all look the same, what students did beyond class
        carries the weight.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shift">
      <div class="rv">
        <p class="body">
          Twenty years ago the average admitted student at UBC had 70%.
          Today it's 87%. The same shift shows up at most major Canadian
          universities.
        </p>
        <p class="quote">
          When the top quarter of grades all look the same, the record has
          to separate them.
        </p>
        <p class="body">
          Universities now adjust grades by school and look harder at
          confirmed work. Employers do the same. The record has to start
          earlier.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="chart rv d1"
        aria-label="UBC average entrance grade, 70 percent in 2004, 87 percent in 2024"
      >
        <h4>UBC average entrance grade</h4>
        <p class="s">Then vs now, twenty years apart</p>
        <div class="bars">
          <div class="bcol"><b>70%</b><i data-h="56"></i></div>
          <div class="bcol now"><b>87%</b><i data-h="70"></i></div>
        </div>
        <div class="blab"><span>2004</span><span>2024</span></div>
        <span class="delta">+17 points</span>
        <small>Source: Fraser Institute, 2024</small>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec soft">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag">The grades problem</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Why grades alone no longer work</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        The data has moved in one direction for two decades.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="trio">
      <div class="tr3 rv">
        <div class="k">Adj.</div>
        <span class="kl">Applied school by school</span>
        <h4>Admissions adjustment</h4>
        <p>
          Waterloo Engineering adjusts grades to compare high schools
          fairly.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://uwaterloo.ca/engineering/future-students"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >University of Waterloo</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="tr3 rv d1">
        <div class="k">+17</div>
        <span class="kl">UBC entrance grade, 20 years</span>
        <h4>Grade inflation</h4>
        <p>From 70% to 87%. The same trend shows up across Canada.</p>
        <a
          href="https://www.fraserinstitute.org/commentary/grade-inflation-gives-students-false-sense-of-their-academic-abilities"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >Fraser Institute, 2024</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="tr3 rv d2">
        <div class="k">−35</div>
        <span class="kl">PISA points, 2003 to 2022</span>
        <h4>Achievement decline</h4>
        <p>Math scores fell about a full grade level while grades rose.</p>
        <a href="https://www.oecd.org/pisa/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >OECD PISA, via Fraser Institute</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="short rv">
      <b>The short version:</b> grades went up, measured achievement went
      down. The record students build outside class fills the gap.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec dark">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag on-dark">Future of work</span>
      <h2 class="h2">What's rising, and what's falling</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        The rising skills are about thinking, leading, and learning. Not
        specific tools.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rf">
      <div class="rfc up rv">
        <h4>
          Rising by 2030
          <small
            style="
              font-family: var(--b);
              font-size: 12px;
              font-weight: 700;
              padding: 3px 9px;
              border-radius: 999px;
              background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
              color: #fff;
            "
            >Illustrative</small
          >
        </h4>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <span>AI and big data</span><i><em data-wv="92"></em></i>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Creative thinking</span><i><em data-wv="80"></em></i>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Resilience and flexibility</span
            ><i><em data-wv="74"></em></i>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Leadership</span><i><em data-wv="68"></em></i>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rfc down rv d1">
        <h4>
          Falling by 2030
          <small
            style="
              font-family: var(--b);
              font-size: 12px;
              font-weight: 700;
              padding: 3px 9px;
              border-radius: 999px;
              background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
              color: #fff;
            "
            >Illustrative</small
          >
        </h4>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <span>Customer service</span><i><em data-wv="40"></em></i>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Manual dexterity</span><i><em data-wv="55"></em></i>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>Routine reading and writing</span
            ><i><em data-wv="62"></em></i>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="rf-note rv">
      Skill direction from the World Economic Forum, Future of Jobs 2025.
      Bar lengths are illustrative, not WEF figures.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" id="sources">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head rv">
      <span class="tag">Sources we cite</span>
      <h2 class="h2">The reports behind Y2O</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        All public. No paywalls between you and the source.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="srcs">
      <div class="sx rv d0">
        <div class="top"><span>Skills</span><b>39%</b></div>
        <h4>World Economic Forum</h4>
        <small>Future of Jobs Report · 2025</small>
        <p>Core skills expected to change by 2030.</p>
        <a
          href="https://www.weforum.org/publications/the-future-of-jobs-report-2025/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >weforum.org →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="sx rv d1">
        <div class="top"><span>Youth</span><b>914K</b></div>
        <h4>Government of Canada / ESDC</h4>
        <small>Labour market · 2025</small>
        <p>Youth 15 to 29 not in school, work, or training.</p>
        <a
          href="https://search.open.canada.ca/qpnotes/record/esdc-edsc%2CFCY_JUN2025_005"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >canada.ca →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="sx rv d2">
        <div class="top"><span>Admissions</span><b>87%</b></div>
        <h4>Fraser Institute</h4>
        <small>Entrance grade report · 2024</small>
        <p>UBC average entrance grade, up from 70%.</p>
        <a
          href="https://www.fraserinstitute.org/commentary/grade-inflation-gives-students-false-sense-of-their-academic-abilities"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >fraserinstitute.org →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="sx rv d0">
        <div class="top"><span>Ontario</span><b>40h</b></div>
        <h4>Ontario Ministry of Education</h4>
        <small>Secondary School Diploma</small>
        <p>
          Community involvement needed to graduate. The floor, not the
          ceiling.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.ontario.ca/page/get-your-high-school-volunteer-hours"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >ontario.ca →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="sx rv d1">
        <div class="top"><span>Admissions</span><b>Adj.</b></div>
        <h4>University of Waterloo</h4>
        <small>Engineering admissions</small>
        <p>School-by-school adjustment to incoming grades.</p>
        <a
          href="https://uwaterloo.ca/engineering/future-students"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          >uwaterloo.ca →</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="sx rv d2">
        <div class="top"><span>Achievement</span><b>−35</b></div>
        <h4>OECD PISA</h4>
        <small>2003 to 2022 · math</small>
        <p>Canadian math scores down about a full grade level.</p>
        <a href="https://www.oecd.org/pisa/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >oecd.org →</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="disc rv">
      <b>Informed by, not endorsed by.</b> These organizations are not
      affiliated with Y2O and do not endorse it.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec soft">
  <div class="wrap faq">
    <div class="rv">
      <span class="tag">FAQ</span>
      <h2 class="h2">Questions about the research</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size: 18px">
        Still wondering?
        <a
          href="mailto:info@youth2opportunities.ca"
          style="color: var(--maroon); font-weight: 700"
          >info@youth2opportunities.ca</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="qa rv d1">
      <details open>
        <summary>
          Do these organizations endorse Y2O?<span class="pl">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          No. We cite their public research. They are not affiliated with
          Y2O.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          Do you commission your own research?<span class="pl">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          No. We don't commission reports and then quote them as
          independent.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>
          Why include grade inflation?<span class="pl">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p>
          It shows why grades alone are a weaker signal than they used to
          be.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Are the sources linked?<span class="pl">+</span></summary>
        <p>Yes. Every number on this page links to its public source.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding: 0 0 40px">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta rv">
      <div>
        <span class="tag on-dark">Build with the data in mind</span>
        <h2>Start before the record is needed</h2>
        <p>Live now across Ontario.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="contact.html"
          >Create your account</a
        ><a class="btn btn-line-light" href="about.html">About Y2O</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script is:inline>
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-h]").forEach(function (e) {
    new IntersectionObserver(
      function (es, o) {
        if (es[0].isIntersecting) {
          e.style.height = e.dataset.h + "%";
          o.disconnect();
        }
      },
      { threshold: 0.4 },
    ).observe(e);
  });
</script>
  <Reveal slot="scripts" />
</Base>
